.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-task-register 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-task\-register \- Record that a task has started, under its pid
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten task register\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fItask\fR> <\fIpid\fR> [\fIphase\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Record that a task has started, under its pid
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fItask\fR>
The task\*(Aqs name, as its callers know it
.TP
<\fIpid\fR>
The process the record is keyed by
.TP
[\fIphase\fR]
What the task is doing; absent is `starting`
